One day, a terrible drought began. The Sun's fire grew so fierce it started consuming itself. The Sun realized it needed the Ocean's cooling mists to survive.

"Deep Ocean," called the Sun, "I will send down my light and warmth. With it, you can create rising vapors that will save us both."

The Ocean was suspicious. "How do I know you won't simply steal my waters and leave me empty?"

