The Ocean considered the Sun's vulnerability in making this offer. Finally, it accepted the light and warmth. The waters rose as vapor, and true to the Ocean's nature, it returned more than half—sending rain to nourish the lands between them.

From that day forward, the Sun and Deep learned that reciprocity creates abundance, while hoarding breeds only scarcity.

And so the water cycle was born from an act of trust.
